output.text:
Read recent status and turn summaries for one thread or chat without opening it. Use page cursors from earlier responses to read older turns. This tool is part of plugin `codex-app-tools`.

Manage the Codex desktop app: find, create, and update chats; organize projects, sidebar, and pinned items; schedule automations; manage worktrees; open app panels; and locate bundled libraries for documents, spreadsheets, slides, and PDFs.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_app__read_thread(args: {
  // Optional cursor for older turns.
  cursor?: string;
  // Optional host id returned by create_thread or list_threads.
  hostId?: string;
  // Whether to include truncated tool or command outputs.
  includeOutputs?: boolean;
  // Maximum characters to keep for each included Codex output, command, tool argument preview, or chat message. Oversized tool arguments return a text preview.
  maxOutputCharsPerItem?: number;
  // Thread id to inspect.
  threadId: string;
  // Maximum number of turns to return.
  turnLimit?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
